  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda: Contribute to the Development of a National Labour Migration Policy and Review of Existing Bilateral Labour Migration Agreements (BLMAs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the Ministry of Gender Labour and Social Development in developing a road map towards a labour migration policy as well as review the existing bilateral labour migration agreements (BLAs). The project will be conducting a situation analysis followed by data collection from the major stakeholders (migrant workers&apos; associations, national institutions, trade unions, employers&apos; associations, etc.) and assessing the existing BLAs signed by Uganda in view of contributing to better analysis of the implementation of those BLAs. The project will also aim to conduct a regulatory impact assessment to inform policy decision. Recommendations from the Regional Ministerial Forum on Migration (RMFM) on Harmonizing Labour Migration Policies in East and Horn of Africa, Uganda is one of the co-signatories of this process and proposed the strengthening of labour migration governance through priority actions for effective labour migration policy development and drafting, negotiating and implementing BLAs.</narrative>
  </description>
